-- title:
--   Wide two-branch normalisation at supersingular nodes with j∈{0,1728}
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q\ge 5$, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$, and let $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose vanishing locus is exactly the maximal ideal of $A$ (hypothesis `hker`). Let $a\in k$ satisfy: $a\in$ `ssJSet q k`, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $k$ with $j$-invariant $a$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$; $a^{q^2}=a$; and $a=0$ or $a=1728$. Let $f$ be a nonzero element of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$q$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$-Laurent series. Assume (hypothesis `hford`) that $W.\mathrm{ord}\,f=0$ for every place $W$ of this field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which is centred at the pair $(a,a^{q})$, meaning that there are $x,y\in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x=a$, $\mathrm{red}\,y=a^{q}$ and $W.\mathrm{ord}(j-x)>0$, $W.\mathrm{ord}(j\circ q\text{-expansion}-y)>0$, where $j$ denotes the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` and the second element the image of `qExpand ℚ (1 * q) jq`. Set $e=$ `jWidth a`, which is $3$ if $a=0$ and $2$ if $a=1728$. The conclusion produces $c\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $c\ne 0$ and $m\in\mathbb Z$ with $e\mid m$ such that: the Laurent series of $c\cdot f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the level-$q$ modular ring with $A$-integral coefficients at the prime cut out by $\mathrm{red}$; the Laurent series of the Fricke involute `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)` of $(c\,q^{m})\cdot f$ lies in the same subring; the image of $c\cdot f$ under the reduction homomorphism `modularRedLocHom (1 * q) A.toSubring red` lies in `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`, the $k$-subfield of $k$-Laurent series generated by `jqModC k` and `jqNModC k 1`; both reductions (of $c\cdot f$ and of the Fricke involute) are nonzero; and finally $e\cdot \mathrm{ord}\,\overline{c f}=-m$, the order being taken at the first component of `frobNodePair q a`, that is at the place `charLGeomPlaceOfPoint k a` of `modularFunctionFieldC k 1`.
--
--   This is the two-branch normalisation step in the analysis of the reduction of $X_0(q)$ modulo $q$ at a supersingular crossing point whose $j$-invariant is $0$ or $1728$, where the node has width $e=3$ or $e=2$ rather than $1$: a function with neither zero nor pole at the node can be scaled to be a unit on the branch through $\infty$, and simultaneously, after multiplying by a power $q^{m}$ with $e\mid m$ and applying the Fricke involution, on the branch through $0$, the jump $m$ being $-e$ times the order of the reduced function at the node. It is used by the lemmas identifying the annuli around such nodes with the standard charts at level one.
